WHY Starts the main chassis with 2 triangle beams and 2 friction pins. It sits toward the rear of the truck, low on the truck. Nothing from earlier steps is touched yet, so this starts a new sub-assembly that later steps will join up. The friction pins grip the triangle beam with friction, making a rigid join (4 such joints in this step). Its unused ends stay free because step 5 slots 2 motors onto them.
