WHY Adds a 7-hole beam, a 3-hole beam, 2 16-tooth gears, a 5-long axle, 2 axle connectors and 2 other parts to the main chassis. It sits at the rear of the truck, at mid height. It is fixed onto the 2 7-long axles from step 17 and 5-long stop axle from step 16. The 7-long axle is locked in the cross hole of the 16-tooth gear, so the two turn together (4 such joints in this step). The 7-long axle passes through a round hole of the 7-hole beam with no grip, so it can spin or swing freely there (6 such joints in this step). The two 16-tooth gears mesh 1:1, so speed is unchanged and the direction reverses. These parts are on the drive line from the drive motor, so they must stay locked on their axles and turn freely in their bearings. Its unused end stays free because step 22 slots a 3x5 L-beam onto it.
STEP 19
ADD powe-motor-1 21980 white
